From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: computerguy526 <355510486+computerguy526@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 11:22:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] kosmickrisp: compute loop cap (default on), AccessRevoked
 classifier, first-OOM dump

On macOS committed Metal command buffers keep running after the process
exits (NXNative issue #2664), so the gpusafe watchdog + _exit does not stop
a runaway shader loop. Loops that end by themselves do.

Loop cap: port of the design of NXNative commit bb574c7 "chain/compute:
contain runaway loops and report capped kernels"
(https://github.com/seedds/nxnative, MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 seedds;
co-authored by FifteenPen, computerguy526 and uncraftablexd, PRs #2254 and
#2709) to the NIR -> MSL path:
- application compute kernels only; KK_LOOP_CAP = loop-condition checks per
  kernel invocation, default 2^18, 0 = off (replaces the opt-in per-loop
  KK_LOOP_CAP of the previous commit); the budget is shared by all loops of
  the kernel (KK prints one function per kernel);
- the first thread that exhausts its budget stores 1 to a GPU-side abort
  word of the command buffer and records its loop site (atomic min) in the
  kernel's hit word; other loops poll the abort word every 1024 checks;
- a loop containing an execution barrier (directly, nested, or through a
  callee) has a private counter that restarts at each loop entry and never
  reads the abort word;
- the loop state (16 bytes per kernel per command buffer, pool owned by
  kk_safety) is bound at argument table slot 3; the completion handler logs
  "[RED] loop cap hit: submission, kernel <msl blake3>, loop site" once per
  kernel.

gpusafe fixes, following NXNative's gpu_lost_check / res_top_once:
- AccessRevoked only for MTL4CommandQueueErrorDomain, searched through
  underlying errors to depth 3 (an innocent victim's IOGPU code 5 no longer
  counts); recorded waiter events are raised before the exit;
  KK_TEST_GPU_LOST=<n> / KK_TEST_OOM=<n> inject the feedback without a GPU
  fault; KK_QUEUE_ERROR_EXIT=0 halts without exiting;
- the first OutOfMemory failure dumps KK's memory by owner, the 24 largest
  allocation sizes, Metal's allocated / recommended sizes and the residency
  set totals (KK_OOM_DUMP=0 off);
- the residency limit is set at the first commit when the guards were
  initialized by a dispatch recorded earlier (it stayed 0 = off).

Tests: src/kosmickrisp/compiler/tests/loopcap_nir_test.c (target
kk_loopcap_nir_test, GPU-free); work/s3/kk-safe/test/run_unit.sh;
work/kyty/loopcap/run_gpu.sh (bounded on-GPU).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
